Package: mc-server
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: any
Maintainer: Dylan Bulmer <dylan@bulmer.dev>
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: mc-rcon, mc-backup, mc-mrpack
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://apt.bulmer.dev
Description: Minecraft server lifecycle manager
 mc manages a single Minecraft server instance on bare metal, or inside a VM,
 LXC container or Docker image. It installs and upgrades Vanilla, Paper, Fabric
 and NeoForge servers, drives the systemd lifecycle, and owns the server's
 configuration.
 .
 Java (8, 17, 21 or 25) is selected automatically from the requested Minecraft
 version, including Mojang's 26.x versioning scheme.
 .
 mc is plugin-first: a plugin is another .deb that drops a manifest into
 /usr/lib/mc/plugins.d/ and contributes subcommands and lifecycle hooks. The
 recommended set is mc-rcon (console, graceful shutdown), mc-backup (backups and
 restores) and mc-mrpack (Modrinth modpacks). Run 'mc plugins' to see what is
 installed.
 .
 Installing a server requires accepting the Minecraft EULA, either interactively
 or with 'mc install --accept-eula'. The server will not start until it has been.
